WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:09.639
Bangladesh is the World’s best country…

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:11.980
if you don’t want to be alone.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.020
This country has half of the population of
America but concentrated inside an area the

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.020
size of Illinois.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.119
It is the most densely populated country on
the planet.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.440
This is also one of the fastest growing countries
in the last two decades.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.840
In less than 20 years, Bangladesh has cut
poverty in half.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:35.040
Today, they are the leader in textile manufacturing,
only surpassed by China.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.600
In fact, I’m sure your shirt, your trousers
or something else you’re wearing today is

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.600
made here.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.879
But wait a minute because it is still too
soon to open the champagne bottle!

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:46.340
Yes, Bangladesh grows fast.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.969
But still today, 13% of their population lives
on less than 2 dollars a day.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:53.769
That’s 20 million people.

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:58.159
Add to this the fact that Islam is the main
religion in the country and you have headlines

00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:00.920
like this one.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:07.470
Terrorist activity increased in Bangladesh
in 2016 amid global fall in attacks

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.690
Despite the fact that Bangladesh has a secular
constitution, adulterous women are stoned

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:13.570
to death in some regions.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:18.420
And 80% of the population agrees with changing
the legislation so it meets the principles

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.580
of SHARIA law.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.830
Meanwhile, despite the radicalism of some
citizens, the prime minister, SHEIKH HASINA,

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:24.930
is a woman.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:28.300
And the opposition leader, KHALEDA ZIA, is
also a woman.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.340
So the situation is far from quiet.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:35.220
Especially given that in the next year, 2018,
Bangladesh will hold elections that might

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.570
be crucial for the future of this country.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.700
So the question to be made here is…

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.510
Can Bangladesh become an Islamic Republic?

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:50.980
Why do we think Bangladesh is a demographic
bomb?

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:54.990
Today we are going to answer these questions,
but before we do, let’s take a look back

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.180
at history.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.600
ONE COUNTRY, TWO FAMILIES

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.250
In 1947, the British Empire let the Indian
colonies become independent.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:10.760
The parts where HINDUISM was the main religion
became what today is INDIA.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:18.090
The parts with an Islamic majority became
PAKISTAN.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.439
But things are not as simple as they seem.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:23.739
The Muslim part ended up divided into two
parts.

00:02:23.739 --> 00:02:27.349
As you can see on the screen, India was in
the middle, and to the left and right there

00:02:27.349 --> 00:02:31.170
was Pakistan, with a political system based
on Sharia law.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.489
2,200 kilometres divided these two parts that
belonged to the same state.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:38.730
As you can imagine, this just couldn’t work
properly.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:42.659
In fact, putting aside the fact that they
had the same religion, these two parts had

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:43.670
nothing in common.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:50.180
They didn’t even speak the same language.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:55.620
Western Pakistanis despised the Eastern Pakistanis,
also known as the bengalies, wanted to have

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:56.890
their own country as well.

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:02.860
So in 1971 the Liberation War started.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:08.459
Estimates say that between 300,000 and 3 million
civilians died in this war.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:11.700
But, as a result, a brand new country was
born.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.540
And this was the People’s Republic of Bangladesh.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:20.379
This is also how MUJIBUR RAHMAN, or as they
know him, BANGABANDHU, became the first president.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:25.790
So since Pakistan was an islamic country and
Bangladesh hated Pakistan badly, Bangabandhu

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.480
designed a constitution that was completely
secular.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.840
In fact, they followed the ideological fashion
of the time, so called ARAB SOCIALISM.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:39.819
This was an ideological cocktail that combined
authoritarian leaders, centralized economy

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.560
and secularism.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.790
But wait a minute because it was not that
easy.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.379
4 years later, BANGABANDHU and his whole family
died in a coup d’etat made by those who

00:03:53.379 --> 00:03:57.140
supported Pakistani rule during the Liberation
war.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.159
Only his two daughters survived.

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:01.700
One of them, SHEIKH HASINA is the current
prime minister.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.969
But let’s get back to the coup d’etat.

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:09.159
After two years of political stability and
the influence of the CIA, General ZIAUR RAHMAN

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:15.799
became the man in charge.

00:04:15.799 --> 00:04:20.680
One of his most controversial decisions was
to give amnesty to the pro Pakistani, and

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.620
therefore, islamist soldiers who killed Bangabandhu.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:27.780
This is how the big ideological divide was
created in Bangladesh.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.131
On one hand, we have the family and the political
party of General RAHMAN, the BNP or Bangladesh

00:04:32.131 --> 00:04:33.530
National Party.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.280
They are a conservative coalition with a strong
presence among islamist parties.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:43.200
Some of those who participated in the coup
d´etat in 1975 became members of this BNP

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.200
party.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:49.070
On the other hand, we have the party of BANGABANDHU,
the so-called AWAMI LEAGUE that can be considered

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:57.500
socialist and secularist.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.840
General Rahman ruled the country for 4 years.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.200
Then, of course, came another coup d´etat.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:07.040
Bangladesh was ruled by the military until
1991, when democracy came back to the country.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:14.660
But wait a minute because the Bangladesh way
of democracy is far from democratic…

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.000
ONE COUNTRY, TWO WOMEN

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.700
Since 1991, those two political parties had
two main leaders.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.960
On the BNP side, we have KHALEDA ZIA, the
widow of ZIAUR RAHMAN.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.980
On the Awami side there is Sheikh HASINA,
the daughter of BANGABANDHU.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.570
Since then, elections have been a fight between
two women that alternate in power every 5

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.570
years.

00:05:36.570 --> 00:05:39.310
Neither one of them can win the elections
consistently.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.510
In fact, elections in Bangladesh are absolute
hell.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:52.790
Usually, the opposition party organizes violent
protests and never ending strikes that paralyze

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.970
the country.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:58.910
But in 2006, things changed.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:03.740
Back then, the Awami league, led by Sheikh
Hasina disagreed with the way they organized

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.960
the elections.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.970
This was business as usual.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:11.640
But this time, the military tried to make
a coup d´etat to put some order in the country

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.650
like they had in the 80s.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.710
Elections had to be postponed for two years.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.420
And finally, Sheikh Hasina, won the elections.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.960
In that moment, Hasina learnt a lesson: the
important thing is not winning the office

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:23.970
but keeping it.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:30.590
Remember when I told you that General Rahman
gave amnesty to those who killed BANGABANDHU

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:31.840
40 years before?

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.850
Well… his daughter Sheick Hasina had a good
memory.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:40.800
And she took those memories from the past
to sue all those islamists who might challenge

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:47.460
her power, those who participated in the 1975
coup d´etat.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.190
BANGLADESH EXECUTES LEADER OF LARGEST ISLAMIST
PARTY

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.190
MOTIUR RAHMAN NIZAMI HANGED FOR CRIMES COMMITTED
DURING 1971 WAR OF INDEPENDENCE WITH PAKISTAN

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:56.520
If this wasn’t enough, she broke one of
the biggest political traditions in Bangladesh.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:00.520
Usually, during an elections, the parliament
would create a neutral government in order

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.290
to guarantee a clean and fair process.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.450
But Hasina was not willing to leave power.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:07.390
The opposition boycotted the elections.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:13.430
And Hasina won with 79% of the vote.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.810
BANGLADESH RULING PARTY WINS AFTER BOYCOTTED
VOTE

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.670
In other words…

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.900
now, in 2017, Sheikh Hasina is the strongest
leader in Bangladesh history.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:27.340
And this is no little thing if we remember
this is a country of more than 160 million

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.340
inhabitants.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.470
So the question now is… is there anyone
who can match Hasina’s power?

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:39.430
Well… the answer is YES.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.430
DEMOGRAPHIC BOMB

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:45.210
As we said at the beginning, over 20 million
Bangladeshi citizens live in extreme poverty.

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:47.530
They are young and extremely religious.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:52.520
In other words, they are the perfect market
for a radical islamist movement.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.090
And yes, you might say now…

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:58.090
‘But, Simon, Didn’t you say Bangladesh
is one of the fastest growing countries?’

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.090
Yes!

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:06.560
This is exactly why those 20 million poor
citizens are a real problem.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:14.900
Listen, if you want to start a populist revolution,
never go to an extremely poor country.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:19.030
In fact, most of the radical movements appear
when countries are starting to grow or are

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.800
stepping out of a crisis.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.680
That’s your window of opportunity.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.580
That is the moment when the worse off citizens
can feel jealous of those who are getting

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:28.370
wealthier and wealthier.

00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:33.070
Those 20 million impoverished citizens are
a perfect target for radicalization.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.269
And a real threat to the country’s stability.

00:08:36.269 --> 00:08:40.700
This is why terrorist attacks have been getting
more and more frequent in Bangladesh since

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:46.440
2013.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.550
Many of the victims are bloggers who claim
to be atheists and tried to spread secularism

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.650
in the country.

00:08:51.650 --> 00:09:00.680
But the real wake up call came in 2016.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:06.230
Bangladesh attack: Isis gunmen kill at least
22 people in hostage crisis at Dhaka restaurant

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:09.450
Since then, Sheikh Hasina has been trying
to stop terrorism.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.900
Nonetheless, as I said, in 2018, elections
will be held.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:17.250
And the government is trying to gain support
from that religious population.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:21.490
This is why Hasina is letting Saudi Arabia
invest 1 billion dollars into the building

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.830
of 560 mosques throughout the country.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.690
At the same time, she is making it harder
for women to inherit money and easier for

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:32.900
minor girls to get married to much older men.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:42.140
But not only that!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:47.450
An Islamic propaganda group called HEFAZAT-E-ISLAM
sent their agenda with 13 political suggestions

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.950
to the government .
For instance, they wanted the religious teachings

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:56.140
given at radical mosques to be considered
at the same level as any academic institution.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:10:01.810
And, against the odds, Sheikh Hasina has accepted
that and other proposals from the radicals.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:05.300
Don’t forget that she and her party are
the ones that stand for the secular values

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:13.460
against a more traditional approach from the
BNP party.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:18.570
So this leads to the big question here…

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:23.020
Do you think Bangladesh is at risk of becoming
a de facto Islamic republic?

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:27.690
Or is this just a political game for Sheikh
Hasina to strengthen her power before the

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.690
elections?

